2026-11-08T22:15:01.5710466Z   ok   no topic and an offset entity: one publish of 5 sends one set_value of 5 (R10-GENERIC-HEAT-CURVE)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5710632Z   ok   the entity option empty: no set_value, and the /set topic still carries the integer (W7)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5710809Z   ok   both configured: MQTT first with the full integer, the entity bounded by the 3 K default band
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5710958Z   ok   a kelvin entity is sent -2 for -2, never 271.15 through the absolute helpers (T1)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5711116Z   ok   a Fahrenheit entity is sent the difference x9/5: 2 K is 3.6 °F (T1)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5711286Z   ok   an entity range narrower than the displace saturates and is latched once, naming it (W6)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5711381Z   ok   a reading already at the target is not written (W1)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5711523Z   ok   inside the grace a differing reading proves nothing: no second write (W2)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5711634Z   ok   after the grace the first miss is written once more (W2)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5711765Z   ok   a second miss for the same target latches a warning and sends nothing (W3)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5711854Z   ok   and a new target is written again (W3)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5711985Z   ok   the 24 h write guard is 2 x 1440 / interval: 96 at the default 30 min (W4)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5712136Z   ok   at the guard nothing is written and it is latched; one below it the write goes (W4)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5712513Z   ok   absent, unavailable, a non-temperature unit, a sensor, a range without 0 or a raising service: no value lands, the failure is latched, the MQTT arm still publishes
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5712614Z   ok   MODE_OFF after a write writes one 0 (the off rule)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5712722Z   ok   and while off the arm writes nothing, nor does a second off
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5712865Z   ok   nothing written, nothing restored; an unconfigured entity is never written
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5713007Z   ok   unload after a write writes one 0, through async_unload_entry (the off rule)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5713133Z   ok   a write left armed by a crash is restored by the next run's first off
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5713442Z   ok   a stand-in second consumer registers without editing the hook: its baseline, captured before its first write, survives a restart and is what the restore writes
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5713596Z   ok   and an unreadable baseline refuses the consumer's write: nothing to restore it to
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5713886Z   ok   an unregistered consumer, or one its factory reads as unconfigured, refuses the write and leaves no record behind
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5714064Z   ok   a restore whose write raises sends nothing, stays armed and latches a warning naming the entity
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5714205Z   ok   and the next off retries it: one write of the neutral 0, disarmed and counted
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5714390Z   ok   an armed consumer no longer configured is disarmed unwritten: its entity is not the optimizer's
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5714559Z   ok   a store that cannot save still arms the write, and one that cannot be removed does not raise
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5714760Z   ok   T2 at its bounds: a range starting or ending at 0 is an offset, one starting at 0.5 or ending at -0.5 is not
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5714900Z   ok   every refusal of the pure convert names why and is never read as saturated
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5715056Z   ok   a range narrower than the displace saturates on the low side too: -3 K sends -2 (W6)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5715250Z   ok   a reading exactly half a step from the target holds: 2.25 against 2 at step 0.5 is not written (W1)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5715467Z   ok   a target within half a step of the last write is that write, still in its grace: 3 after 2 at step 2 sends nothing (W2)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5715839Z   ok   a reading that held clears the misses, and the grace is 90 s: a miss 91 s after the write is written once more, not given up (W1, W2)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5716009Z   ok   writes older than 24 h leave the guard: a full day of them 24 h and 1 s old blocks nothing (W4)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5716154Z   ok   at exactly 90 s the grace is over: a miss then is written once more (W2's bound)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5716343Z   ok   and a write exactly 24 h old still counts: a full day of them at that age blocks the write (W4's bound)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5716504Z   ok   the entity arm answers True only for a write sent: held, capped and unreadable are False
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5716748Z   ok   a write that succeeds clears the failure latch, and so does a readable entity: the next failure is warned again, not swallowed
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5716922Z   ok   the heat-curve diagnostics: zeros before any write, the write and its 24 h count after one
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5717087Z   ok   publish called without mode_off writes the entity: only the off mode suppresses the arm
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5717243Z   ok   a restore that succeeded cleared its latch: the next failed restore is warned again
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5717364Z   ok   and after the retry succeeds no failure is held for that consumer
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5717522Z   ok   a write the restore hook refuses to arm is never sent: the arm refuses before the write
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5717713Z   ok   a heat-curve write armed before its entity option was cleared is disarmed unwritten at the next off
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5717863Z   ok   a mode change that is not into off, or off to off, restores nothing and answers 0
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5718169Z   ok   a restore is persisted, so the next run does not restore it again; a forgotten entry's armed set is gone from the store
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5718295Z   ok   the persisted armed set is read once per entry, not at every arm
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5718481Z   ok   the off-restore store is at version 1: a bump strands every persisted armed set without a migration
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5718615Z   ok   a factory reset keeps the heat-curve kind beside its entity (ghc-d03)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5718888Z   ok   off then on inside the grace, plan unchanged: the re-enable rewrites 2 over the restore's 0, never held as W2's grace of the write before the off
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5719117Z   ok   a rewrite that held, then off and on at the same target: 2 is written again and W3 does not latch against the restore's own 0
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5719304Z   ok   null control, the same history without the off and on: the held 2 is not rewritten, nothing warned
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5719592Z   ok   unload, then the reloaded coordinator for the same entry inside the grace: 2 is written over the restore's 0
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5719772Z   ok   a re-enable at 0 right after a restore that did not hold is inside the restore's own grace (W2)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5719980Z   ok   and after its grace the restore's first miss is written once more, not given up on the plan's earlier miss (W3)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5720117Z   ok   a restore whose write raised leaves the arm's record at the plan's write
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5720295Z   ok   the peak guard's engage writes the plan less the nudge to the entity, its release the plan again
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5720482Z   ok   boost writes the displace maximum to the entity, the boost mode and the space boost overlay alike
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5720659Z   ok   the learned curve bias reaches the entity: 3 with a -1 bias sends 2; with curve learning off, 3
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5720831Z   ok   the chokepoint called while off writes no entity value; the MQTT arm still carries the integer
