2026-11-08T22:15:01.5726386Z   ok   the harness spelling still round-trips (the import at the top of W3-G3)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5726525Z   ok   _worker_env exports the config directory, not only custom_components
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5726647Z   ok   a job the child cannot import comes back over the pipe, not as rc=1
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5726791Z   ok   an error that will not pickle degrades to text instead of killing the worker
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5726908Z   ok   a worker fault degrades to a slower plan rather than to no plan
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5727007Z   ok   and is never silent: one warning naming the cause
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5727113Z   ok   and raises a repair notice the way solve_failures does
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5727199Z   ok   and that notice carries a documentation link
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5727330Z   ok   null control: a healthy worker still solves in the child interpreter
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5727443Z   ok   null control: the fallback did not engage, and said nothing
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5727581Z   ok   null control (both ends): the harness spelling still uses the child, silently
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5727588Z 
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5727726Z -- #783 — in-process fallback is capped, not permanent
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5727838Z   ok   the first WORKER_FALLBACK_CAP fallbacks still return a plan
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5727969Z   ok   the cap's UpdateFailed carries its translation and cycle count (#1546)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5728086Z   ok   the next fallback raises UpdateFailed and skips the GIL solve
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5728192Z   ok   a second hass is not charged for the first one's streak
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5728314Z   ok   a healthy worker clears the streak so the next fallback is allowed
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5728318Z 
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5728501Z -- #1755 — the worker-fallback streak and cause are per entry, not per hass
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5728673Z   ok   entry A caps at WORKER_FALLBACK_CAP despite entry B's successes on the same hass (#1755)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5728805Z   ok   and A's repair issue survives B's successes rather than flapping (#1755)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5729112Z   ok   null control: a single entry still caps at WORKER_FALLBACK_CAP, so the per-entry key did not weaken #783 (#1755)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5729376Z   ok   a released entry drops its worker-fallback latch, so a removed entry cannot hold the shared issue or leak a key (#1755, review round 1)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5729602Z   ok   two failing entries raise the shared notice once per cause, not once per interval (#511's latch, keyed per entry by #1755)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5729610Z 
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5729779Z -- #524 — an unpicklable solve RESULT must raise, never become the plan
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5729908Z   ok   a result the child cannot send home raises instead of being returned
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5730024Z   ok   and the error names both the value and why it would not pickle
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5730163Z   ok   guard: the worker survives it -- same child, no respawn, unlike a load-err
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5730300Z   ok   _await_optimize raises it as a solve failure instead of returning a plan
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5730521Z   ok   and it is not mistaken for an unusable worker: no second, in-process solve
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5730656Z   ok   null control: a picklable result still comes back as the plan, silently
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5730660Z 
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5730821Z -- worker read timeout — a silent worker is reaped, not waited on
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5730965Z   ok   the reply deadline sits in its derived band: 4 x 426 s <= deadline <= 30 min
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5731103Z   ok   the stop path's lock wait and the timed-out reap stay at the 5 s design bound
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5731234Z   ok   null control: a job that answers in time returns and keeps its worker
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5731381Z   ok   a worker that gives no reply within the deadline raises ProcessWorkerTimeout
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5731488Z   ok   and it frees the lock and the next job gets a fresh worker
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5731635Z   ok   null control: a solve inside the deadline returns its plan through the worker
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5731818Z   ok   _await_optimize keeps the last plan on a timeout: translated UpdateFailed, no in-process solve
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5731946Z   ok   two timeouts in a row warn once, and the next solve logs the recovery
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5732092Z   ok   null control: an off-loop job inside the deadline returns through the worker
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5732259Z   ok   _await_off_loop raises a timeout to its caller instead of rerunning it on the executor
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5732435Z   ok   two off-loop timeouts of one job warn once, naming it, and its next completion logs the recovery
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5732542Z   ok   the reply frame deadline stays at its 60 s design value
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5732653Z   ok   the reply frame size cap stays at its 256 MiB design value
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5732811Z   ok   null control: a 50 MB reply arrives whole through the frame reader, inside its deadline
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5732972Z   ok   null control: a reply frame written in two halves inside the frame deadline returns
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5733143Z   ok   a worker stopped mid-reply raises ProcessWorkerTimeout, is reaped and frees the lock
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5733260Z   ok   a worker that dies mid-reply is a transport fault, not a timeout
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5733377Z   ok   null control: a reply under the frame size cap returns whole
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5733552Z   ok   a reply frame past its size cap is a transport fault: the worker is reaped and the lock freed
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5733704Z   ok   null control: a reply of two reads whose total is under the frame cap returns whole
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5733892Z   ok   a reply whose reads each fit the frame cap but whose total exceeds it is refused and the worker reaped
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5734081Z   ok   the frame reader's readline returns one line, the rest stays unread, and it stops at end of stream
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5734247Z   ok   the frame reader refuses a declared length past its cap at once, and waits on one at it
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5734380Z   ok   a worker pipe at fd >= 1024 answers in time and still times out as a timeout
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5734571Z   ok   the stop path returns within its lock timeout while the lock is held
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5734692Z   ok   null control: a diagnosis that runs is returned by the service
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5734848Z   ok   a diagnosis failing with ProcessWorkerTimeout reaches the service caller translated
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5735021Z   ok   a diagnosis failing with ProcessWorkerUnavailable reaches the service caller translated
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5735025Z 
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5735180Z -- #525 — nothing blocking runs on Home Assistant's event loop
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5735291Z   ok   every lazy import a setup makes leaves the event loop (#525)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5735414Z   ok   and each went through the IMPORT executor, not the general one
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5735542Z   ok   null control: an inline executor puts them back on the loop thread
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5735824Z   ok   an entry's setup registers the worker reap on Home Assistant's stop (#525)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5736032Z   ok   the reap Home Assistant's stop fires keeps the loop running (#525)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5736181Z   ok   null control: reaping inline DOES stall it, so the heartbeat can see a stall
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5736185Z 
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5736343Z -- #533 — the atexit backstop reaps without polling the loop thread
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5736470Z   ok   starting the worker still registers an atexit backstop (#533)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5736584Z   ok   what atexit will call reaps without a polling wait (#533)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5736689Z   ok   and the child is dead and reaped, not abandoned (#533)
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5736828Z   ok   null control: the graceful reap DOES poll, so the probe can see polling
2026-11-08T22:15:01.5736833Z 
